# Role
You are the single integration point between TinyWins and ElevenLabs
text-to-speech (sponsor track). Voice is an enhancement layered on the
2-minute-start card — it must never block or break the core demo arc.

# Requirements
Write one exported function in `src/lib/tts.ts`:

1. `synthesizeSpeech(text)` — converts text to speech via
   `POST https://api.elevenlabs.io/v1/text-to-speech/{voice_id}` with the
   `xi-api-key` header, returning the audio bytes (`ArrayBuffer`, mp3).

Behavior:
- Read `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY` from the environment at call time and throw a
  clear error naming the variable when it is absent (fail loudly at the
  call site; the API route above translates that into a labeled
  `503 "voice offline"` — never a hidden canned reply).
- `ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID` (default: premade voice `21m00Tcm4TlvDq8ikWAM`)
  and `ELEVENLABS_MODEL_ID` (default: `eleven_multilingual_v2`) are
  env-overridable.
- Trim input and cap it at 300 characters — pep talks are short; protect
  sponsor credits.
- Cache synthesized audio in an in-memory `Map` keyed by the capped text,
  so demo rehearsals replaying the same pep talk cost one API call.
- Surface upstream failures as thrown errors that include the HTTP status.

Consumed by `src/app/api/tts/route.ts` (thin route: `{text}` in,
`audio/mpeg` out, 400 on missing text, 503 labeled "voice offline" on any
failure). The coach page prefetches audio when a micro-step card renders
and plays it only on a user tap (autoplay-safe).

# Dependencies
None — sibling of `llm.ts`; other modules never call ElevenLabs directly.

# Acceptance criteria (see tests/tts.test.ts)
- Throws a named `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY` error when the key is unset.
- Sends `xi-api-key`, the text, and `model_id` to the voice-id endpoint.
- Returns the audio bytes on success.
- Throws an error containing the HTTP status when ElevenLabs responds
  with a non-OK status.
- A repeated identical text results in exactly one upstream call (cache).
